          <section><h2>No investment advice</h2><p>Monks Of Market provides general information and mathematical estimates only. Nothing on this site is investment, trading, research, legal, accounting or tax advice; a solicitation or offer; or a recommendation to buy, sell, hold or use any security, derivative, digital asset, broker or exchange.</p></section>
          <section><h2>Derivatives and leverage risk</h2><p>Futures and options are complex, high-risk instruments. Leverage can magnify losses rapidly. You may lose all capital committed to a position and, depending on the product, market gap, liquidation process and account terms, may owe more than the margin posted. Stops may not execute at the selected price.</p><div class="trust-callout"><strong>Never treat “risk budget” as a guaranteed maximum loss.</strong>Slippage, gaps, low liquidity, exchange controls, liquidation mechanics, fees and technical failure can make realized loss larger than the estimate.</div></section>
          <section><h2>Model limitations</h2><p>Outputs depend entirely on the values supplied. Preset charges reflect the stated September 2026 model, not a promise that those rates apply now or to your account. The calculators may omit charges, rebates, tiered pricing, spread, slippage, conversion costs, exercise or assignment effects, penalties, settlement differences and account-specific terms.</p><p>Funding can be paid or received and can change by contract and market conditions. Breakeven results are mathematical estimates and do not account for every execution condition.</p></section>
          <section><h2>Tax and regulatory uncertainty</h2><p>Tax treatment depends on the instrument, transaction structure, jurisdiction and individual circumstances. The applicability of 1% TDS to USDT-settled crypto futures is disputed; the optional TDS field is a cash-withholding scenario, not a conclusion about final tax liability. Consult a qualified professional and current official guidance.</p></section>
          <section><h2>Options-specific risks</h2><p>The options calculator models a premium purchase followed by a premium sale before expiry. It does not model every outcome involving exercise, assignment, physical settlement, margin shortfall, close-out, auto square-off or expiry. In-the-money expiry can lead to materially different STT and settlement consequences.</p></section>
          <section><h2>Third parties</h2><p>Broker, exchange and product names are used for identification. Monks Of Market is not endorsed by, affiliated with or acting for those third parties unless explicitly stated. Verify fees, contract terms, outages and regulatory notices directly with the relevant official source.</p></section>
          <section><h2>Your decision</h2><p>You remain solely responsible for deciding whether to trade and for verifying the suitability, legality and economics of any transaction. Consider obtaining independent professional advice. If you do not understand the product or cannot afford the potential loss, do not trade it.</p></section>
